Use compiler flags qcc accepts in the QNX configure case.

The QNX case sets CFLAGS with "--param=ssp-buffer-size=4", which qcc (the
QNX compiler driver) rejects as an unknown option -- configure then reports
that the C compiler cannot create executables. -fstack-protector-strong
already selects a sensible buffer size. Also drop -I/usr/include/p11-kit-1,
a path of the build host that has no business in a cross build.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -455,7 +455,7 @@
         try_lockmem=1
         feat_refclock=0
         try_recvmmsg=0 # Freebsd "bug" which we inherited. using regular recvmsg makes things work
-        CFLAGS="-O2 -g -fPIE -fstack-protector-strong --param=ssp-buffer-size=4 -Wmissing-prototypes -Wshadow -Wall -pthread -I/usr/include/p11-kit-1"
+        CFLAGS="-O2 -g -fPIE -fstack-protector-strong -Wmissing-prototypes -Wshadow -Wall -pthread"
         add_def QNX
         if [ $feat_droproot = "1" ]; then
           add_def FEAT_PRIVDROP
